# What the two images do not need.
#
# Docker applies this file to the repository-root build context before processing either Dockerfile.
# Excluding generated files and local state makes builds smaller
# and prevents COPY from including development-only data in an intermediate stage.
#
# Dockerfile.backend copies the whole repository to reach the Go sources and vendor/,
# so without this file the database of the development machine,
# the photos it holds and the local node_modules would all be copied into the build
# and end up inside the image.
.git
**/.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
**/.vscode
webui/dist

# State written by a local run, not sources: the image creates its own empty /app/db.
# The default photo is the exception: schemas.DefaultPhotoId names it
# for every user and every group that has no photo of its own,
# and nothing in the code ever writes it,
# so the file itself has to reach the image
db/
!db/photos/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000

# Local validators
validator.md
.spectral.js
.golangci.yml
webui/eslint.config.mjs
webui/node_modules
